# E322 draft - legacy C code fails at link with duplicate symbols under -fno-common

id:                     E322
trigger_tool:           clang|ld.lld|cmake
phase:                  linking
error_signature:        ld\.lld: error: duplicate symbol.*in archive.*|multiple definition of.*|clang.*error: linker command failed

severity:               2
category:               linking, portability, cmake
match_keywords:         duplicate symbol, ld.lld, -fcommon, -fno-common, tentative definition, GCC 10, clang 15, archive, CMake, legacy C code
title:                  Old C code with multiple same-name global definitions needs -fcommon under modern clang/GCC

root_cause:             Pre-2015 C code commonly declares shared lookup tables (e.g. musepack r475 Res_bit/__Cc/__Dc defined in both mpc_decoder.c and requant.c) as multiple "tentative definitions" (int tbl[N]; without extern). Legacy GCC merged them at link time (-fcommon default). GCC >= 10 and modern clang (>= 11, incl. OHOS clang 15) default to -fno-common, so every translation unit emits a real symbol and ld.lld reports duplicate symbol errors when the archive is linked.
affected_scope:         Legacy C/C++ projects (audio codecs, emulators, classic unix tools) that never moved to extern declarations and are built with GCC >= 10 or clang >= 11; hits at the final tool link stage after all static archives build fine.
verification_cmd:       cd build && make 2>&1 | grep "duplicate symbol"; nm libfoo.a | grep " [BbDCd] SYMBOL" shows the symbol defined in several .o of the same archive

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           append-fcommon-flags
rec_description:        Append -fcommon to the project's compiler flags in the least invasive way: for CMake use set(CMAKE_C_FLAGS "${CMAKE_C_FLAGS} ... -fcommon") (append, never overwrite the existing variable so toolchain/env flags survive, R33); for autotools add it to CFLAGS. Verify no symbol is intentionally duplicated across DIFFERENT archives (that would still fail with -fcommon). A cleaner but more invasive alternative is converting the definitions to extern declarations plus a single defining TU - prefer -fcommon for third-party snapshots to keep the patch minimal.
rec_command:            set(CMAKE_C_FLAGS "${CMAKE_C_FLAGS} -O2 -fcommon") # then re-run cmake && make
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               source-patch

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      extern-declaration-refactor
fallback_description:   If -fcommon is unacceptable (e.g. compiler rejects it), refactor the duplicated definitions: keep one defining TU, convert the others to extern declarations; regenerate the patch via refresh-patch --auto.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          source-patch

forbid_1_pattern:       strip.*-fcommon.*from.*flags|-Wl,--allow-multiple-definition
forbid_1_reason:        --allow-multiple-definition masks real ABI bugs by silently picking one definition and hides genuine duplicate-symbol regressions.
forbid_1_consequence:   Shipped binaries may silently use the wrong table/layout, corrupting codec output or crashing at runtime.

principles:             P013
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

doc_file:               drafts/E322-draft-8541.md
last_updated:           2026-09-03
source_event:           musepack r475 adaptation 2026-09-03: ld.lld duplicate symbol Res_bit/__Cc/__Dc from libmpcdec_static.a when linking mpcgain; fixed by appending -fcommon in top-level CMakeLists.txt
authors: ohc-collaborator <8541>
